## Your Task

- **ID**: TASK-260715-1g9cyt
- **Title**: Add extension-safe native dependency packaging seams
- **Parent**: STORY-260715-l2i2oo
### Description

Implement the reproducible packaging and linkage mechanism that later HEV and SSH candidate tasks will use for C and Swift native dependencies in iOS and macOS provider targets and the macOS harness.
### Scope

In scope: source or static-library integration chosen by the ADR; module maps and headers; target triples and architectures; simulator and device variants; compile flags; extension-safe linkage checks; pinned revision inputs; license and notice aggregation hooks; dependency cache policy; a harmless smoke library fixture. Out of scope: integrating HEV, NIOSSH, or libssh2 themselves; dynamic downloads during application runtime; private frameworks; vendored unpinned binaries; and production transport code.
### Acceptance Criteria

1. A pinned harmless native fixture builds and links in iOS simulator, iOS device, macOS provider, shared-core consumer where allowed, and harness configurations. 2. Archive inspection shows no disallowed dynamic library, absolute build path, missing architecture, or extension-unsafe dependency. 3. Revision, source hash, compiler flags, license metadata, and rebuild commands are machine-readable inputs. 4. Dependency updates produce deterministic artifacts and a clear review diff rather than opaque binary replacement. 5. The seam documents how HEV and both SSH candidates plug in without forcing a target-graph redesign.

## Instructions

The following instructions have been attached to this task:

### TASK-260715-1g9cyt_inputs.md
> Native packaging seam requirements

Add extension-safe native-dependency packaging seams so ReluxTunnelCore HEV integration (TASK-260715-1vv52g) can consume the pinned HEV/lwIP baseline. INPUTS: TASK-260715-uopycx audit (pinned unmodified hev-socks5-tunnel ad7600497931205105b08367bd1b450048157e40 + submodules core c234519 / task-system b1afa0e / lwip 2a11c14 / yaml efa3611; upstream build-apple.sh produces an XCFramework with iOS, iOS-Sim, macOS, tvOS, tvOS-Sim slices under Xcode 26.5). .spec/packet-plane.md, security-privacy.md (relay/native supply chain: pinned source, checksum verify, third-party notices), platform-distribution.md (targets iOS 18 / macOS 15 from 3r0993). REQUIREMENTS: package the pinned HEV/lwIP into an EXTENSION-SAFE SPM seam consumable by the Swift core — choose and justify binaryTarget(XCFramework) vs a C-source SwiftPM target; the result must be embeddable in a Network Extension (NO non-embeddable dylibs, NO dlopen/dynamic code loading, static/embeddable linkage) and must NOT pull platform-only frameworks into ReluxTunnelCore proper (keep NE-only concerns in the named adapter/native module, preserving the 2nfz7w boundary + check-core-boundaries). Provide a reproducible vendor/build step that verifies the pinned source by checksum before building (mismatch fails closed) and emits third-party notices. Keep buildable via swift build on macOS; do NOT tune HEV runtime knobs here (that is 1vv52g / M3). If extension-safety cannot be met without a decision (e.g. XCFramework vs source), record options and recommend, do not force-fit.




