The evidence supports a concrete choice: HEV and other custom-build C engines use a locally rebuilt static XCFramework behind a SwiftPM `binaryTarget`; small Swift dependencies remain source packages. The harmless fixture will exercise that exact binary path, while a `ReluxTunnelNativeAdapter` keeps native linkage out of `ReluxTunnelCore` and avoids a later target-graph redesign.
